    managerName: The Eyewitness (traditionally John the Apostle)
    managerFlavorText: An unnamed eyewitness declares what he has heard, seen with
      his own eyes, and touched with his own hands concerning the Word of life, so
      that his readers may share fellowship with him, the Father, and the Son.
    managerUnlockLevel: 3
    managerUnlockAtVerseIndex: 0
    managerBonusMultiplier: 0.25
    managerUnlockCost: 150
    submanagers: []
  - id: walking_in_the_light
    displayName: Walking in the Light
    flavorText: The author teaches that fellowship with God requires walking in his
      light and honestly confessing sin, trusting that Christ's blood cleanses and
      that he stands as advocate and propitiation.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Teaches that fellowship with God requires walking in the light as God
      himself is light, that honest confession of sin (rather than the self-deceiving
      claim to have none) is the true posture of a believer, and that Jesus Christ's
      blood cleanses from sin while he also serves as advocate and propitiation when
      a believer does sin.
    deliveredByManagerId: author_1_john
    managerId: walking_in_the_light
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 24.131744431604677
    costGrowthRate: 1.15
