  - id: love_in_deed_and_truth
    displayName: Love in Deed and in Truth
    flavorText: He commands believers to love not in word but in deed and truth,
      citing Cain's murder of his brother as a warning that hatred is itself murder.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: "Expands on the command to love one another as 'the message that ye
      heard from the beginning,' using Cain as a negative cautionary example (a one-verse
      cross-reference, not indexed as a character in this book \u2014 see genealogyLists)
      and stating that hatred of a brother is itself a form of murder, and teaches
      that real love is proven by sacrificial action \u2014 being willing 'to lay
      down our lives for the brethren' and sharing material goods with a brother
      in need \u2014 'not in word... but in deed and in truth,' linking such love
      to a confident heart before God and to answered prayer."
    deliveredByManagerId: author_1_john
    managerId: love_in_deed_and_truth
    icon: {fileID: 0}
    managerIcon: {fileID: 0}
    baseCost: 4765.6376785461825
